ndemic to the North-western Pacific Ocean (Senou et al. 1987). It is reported to occur from Japan (except northern Hokkaido) through to Ryukyu Islands (Sakai et al. 2001, Senou 2002, Nakae et al. 2018, Sonoyama et al. 2020), Taiwan Province of China (Liu & Shen 1991, Chang et a l. 1999), in the coast of Korean Peninsula (Kim & Kim 1998, Kim et al. 2020) and in mainland China, from Shanghai to Hainan Island (Senou et al. 1987). In the Gulf of Tonkin, it is also available up to Nam Dinh coast in northern Vietnam (Matsunuma in Kimura et al. 2018, this study). Comparisons: Planiliza lauvergnii can be differentiated from P. carinata and P. klunzingeri by its shorter pectoral fin (14 – 18 % of SL vs. 20 – 26 % SL) and smaller head length (22 – 28 % of SL vs. 26 – 31 % of SL) (Senou et al. 1987, this study). The connecting tissue between end of maxillary and mouth corner is ‘ undeveloped’ in P. lauvergnii (vs. well developed in P. caranata and P. klunzingeri; see Senou et al. 1987: Fig. 5).","","text","",""]]},"XLKH":{"v":[["southern pigfish","eng",0],["Peixe-cavalo-austral","por",0],["Sydlig grisefisk","dan",0],["rypáčkovec jižní","ces",0]],"d":[["New Zealand Exclusive Economic Zone","8455","mrgid","",""]]},"XPCL":{"v":[["guaranarana","por",0]],"d":[["Venezuela (Amazonas, Bolívar); Guyana; Surinam; French Guiana; Peru; Bolivia (Beni); N-Brazil (Roraima, Amapa, Pará, Amazonas, Acre); WC-Brazil (Mato Grosso)","","text","",""]]},"ZR9R":{"v":[["skunkweed","eng",0],["Texas croton","",0],["Croton du Texas","fra",0],["K’iniidlishii daa’","nav",0]],"d":[["USA (Alabama, Arizona, Colorado, Delaware, Florida, Iowa, Illinois, Kansas, Massachusetts, Missouri, Nebraska, New Mexico, Oklahoma, South Dakota, Texas, Utah, Wisconsin, Wyoming); Mexico (Chihuahua, Sonora)","","text","",""]]},"ZV25":{"v":[["Swanson's Snake-eyed Skink","eng",0],["Swanson’s snake-eyed skink","eng",0]],"d":[["Australia (Northern Territory)","","text","",""]]},"33FTW":{"d":[["Tanzania","","text","",""]]},"33G3W":{